---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import InstitutionalPage from "../components/InstitutionalPage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Transaction Standards | Quest Luxo"
  description="The principles Quest Luxo applies to private luxury timepiece sourcing and advisory engagements."
  canonicalPath="/transaction-standards"
>
  <InstitutionalPage
    eyebrow="Client Protection"
    title="Transaction Standards"
    intro="Quest Luxo approaches private sourcing through clear authority, documented expectations, proportionate diligence, and client approval."
  >
    <h2>Clear engagement</h2>
    <p>
      Scope, roles, commercial terms, and material assumptions are established
      before a transaction proceeds. A public inquiry is not a commitment by
      either party.
    </p>

    <h2>Item and counterparty diligence</h2>
    <p>
      Diligence is proportionate to the item and transaction. It may include
      identity, provenance, condition, reference, configuration, ownership,
      supplier, logistics, payment, and sanctions-related checks where
      applicable.
    </p>

    <h2>Client decision authority</h2>
    <p>
      Quest Luxo provides information and recommendations, while the client
      retains final decision authority. Material changes in price, condition,
      timing, or transaction structure require renewed client approval.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments and delivery</h2>
    <p>
      Payment instructions, custody, insurance, shipping, inspection, and
      acceptance expectations are confirmed through transaction-specific
      communications. Clients should independently verify payment instructions
      using an established contact channel.
    </p>

    <h2>Concerns</h2>
    <p>
      Transaction questions or concerns may be directed to
      <a href="mailto:contact@questluxo.com">contact@questluxo.com</a>.
    </p>
  </InstitutionalPage>
</BaseLayout>
